# Citation File Format 1.2.0: https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub reads this file directly and renders a "Cite this repository" button on the
# repo, offering APA and BibTeX. Nothing in the build touches it.
#
# This is also the project's author roster. A maintainer is listed here, which is the
# point: it makes co-ownership a citable credit rather than a commit count. Adding a
# maintainer means adding an `authors` entry and a row in GOVERNANCE.md, in the same PR.
#
# `license` names the licence of the citable artifact, which is the registry itself:
# CC-BY-4.0 per LICENSE. The build scripts are MIT, covered separately in that file.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this registry, please cite it as below.
title: "whataifound.org: A Registry of AI Scientific and Mathematical Discoveries"
abstract: >-
  An open, curated registry of scientific and mathematical results produced by or with AI
  systems. Every record is graded on two axes: verification, how solid the evidence is,
  from a machine-checked proof down to refuted; and autonomy, how much the AI did versus
  its human collaborators. Refuted and already-known results stay on the record, marked
  as such.
type: dataset
url: "https://whataifound.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yigitisik/whataifound"
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
version: "2026.07"
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - scientific discovery
  - research verification
  - reproducibility
  - open data
authors:
  - family-names: Isik
    given-names: Mustafa Yigit
